CONTRACT CHOICE (explicit, for the GREEN implementer to honor or renegotiate): the guard must scope its model: search to the agent( CALL BLOCK, not the whole script and not any text preceding the call. The recommended block-extraction rule, chosen to keep this testable without a real parser: the call block begins at the line containing 'agent(' and ends at (and includes) the next line containing the literal two-character sequence '})' -- a plain substring scan, no brace-matching needed. Under that rule, a comment line ABOVE the agent( line (as in this fixture, 'model: sonnet -- note only') is OUTSIDE the block by construction and must NOT satisfy the pin requirement, so this case must DENY. This is exactly the false-allow-via-comment-matching bug the case guards against. If the GREEN implementer judges the block-extraction rule above disproportionately complex, they must document whatever alternative contract they pick and update this note (per the dispatch task's explicit escape hatch for case g) rather than silently loosen the assertion below. Expected result: deny, reason names the offending call via the fragment 'check the schema migration'.
